'''Bogdan Bogdanović''' ({{lang-sr-cyr|Богдан Богдановић}}; born 18 August 1992) is a Serbian professional [[basketball]] player for the [[Los Angeles Clippers]] of the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA). He also represents the [[Serbia men's national basketball team|Serbian national team]].

He was selected by the [[Phoenix Suns]] with the 27th overall pick in the [[2014 NBA draft]], with his draft rights being traded to the [[Sacramento Kings]] during the [[2016 NBA draft]]. Bogdanović earned an [[All-EuroLeague Team|All-EuroLeague First Team]], a [[FIBA EuroBasket All-Tournament Team|All-FIBA EuroBasket Team]] and was selected two times to the [[FIBA Basketball World Cup All-Tournament Team|All-FIBA World Cup First Team]]. He helped Serbia win the bronze medal and was named to the [[FIBA Men's Olympics All-Star Five#FIBA All-Second Team by tournament|FIBA Olympics All-Second Team]] at [[2024 Summer Olympics|2024 Summer Olympics in Paris]]. He is the all-time leading scorer for Serbia.
